    "body": {
      "en": "### Week 1: My Head, Eyes and Mouth\n\nChildren begin with highly visible and familiar body parts on the face and head. The focus is looking, touching, pointing, mirror play, puppet modelling, and simple face routines.\n\n### Week 2: My Hands and Feet\n\nChildren explore hands and feet through clapping, tapping, stamping, touching, showing, washing, mark-making, movement, and body-action games.\n\n### Week 3: Happy, Sad and Angry Faces\n\nChildren begin to recognise basic feeling faces through puppets, mirrors, emotion cards, music, facial expression copying, and teacher-supported comfort routines.\n\n### Week 4: Tired, Rest and Body Care\n\nChildren integrate body and feeling language through rest, calm-down, quiet movement, self-care, baby/teddy care, and simple “all done / rest” routines.",
      "zh": "### Week 1: My Head, Eyes and Mouth｜第一周：我的头、眼睛和嘴\n\n儿童从面部和头部最显眼、最熟悉的身体部位开始。重点是看、触摸、指、镜子游戏、木偶示范和简单的面部常规。\n\n### Week 2: My Hands and Feet｜第二周：我的手和脚\n\n儿童通过拍手、踏步、触摸、展示、洗手、做标记、动作和身体动作游戏来探索手和脚。\n\n### Week 3: Happy, Sad and Angry Faces｜第三周：开心、伤心和生气的脸\n\n儿童通过木偶、镜子、情绪卡片、音乐、面部表情模仿和教师支持下的安抚常规来开始识别基本的表情脸。\n\n### Week 4: Tired, Rest and Body Care｜第四周：累、休息与身体照护\n\n儿童通过休息、冷静、安静动作、自我照护、宝宝／泰迪照护和简单的\"全部完成／休息\"常规把身体和感受语言整合起来。"
    },
