      "en": "### Useful EASTIE Spaces\n\nClassroom  \nMusic classroom  \nTheatre / small dramatic play space  \nIndoor physical fitness area  \nMirror / calm-down area  \nArt classroom  \nCircle-time area / mat area  \nSmall outdoor grass area attached to PG classroom\n\n### Useful Materials\n\nMirrors  \nEmotion cards / feeling face cards  \nPuppets  \nSoft toys  \nBaby dolls  \nDoctor kit  \nScarves  \nRhythm instruments  \nMats  \nBody outline paper  \nCrayons / markers  \nStickers  \nSponge stamps  \nWater wipes / cloths  \nHandwashing visual cards  \nSoft balls / sensory texture balls  \nTeddy bears  \nBlankets\n\n### Enhanced Resource Opportunities\n\nMirrors can support body and feeling recognition without verbal testing. Emotion cards can be used as touch-and-choose materials rather than question-answer tasks. The doctor kit and baby dolls can support care routines. The art classroom can support handprints, face collages, and body-marking activities. The indoor physical space can support body-action songs and simple movement routines.",
