      "en": "This unit should not become an appearance-description unit. PG children do not need to describe hair, eyes, size, or physical traits.\n\nThis unit should not require children to verbalise emotions on demand. Feeling words are introduced through facial expression, gesture, comfort routines, and teacher modelling.\n\nThis unit should not turn body songs into speed or memory tests. Songs should remain slow, gesture-rich, and flexible.\n\nThis unit should avoid shaming or correcting emotions. Sad, angry, and tired should be treated as recognisable human states, with adult support and safe responses.",
      "zh": "本单元不应变成外貌描述单元。PG 儿童不需要描述头发、眼睛、身材或身体特征。\n\n本单元不应要求儿童按需用语言表达情绪。感受词通过面部表情、手势、安抚常规和教师示范引入。\n\n本单元不应把身体歌曲变成速度或记忆测试。歌曲应保持缓慢、手势丰富且灵活。\n\n本单元应避免羞辱或纠正情绪。伤心、生气和累应被视为可识别的人类状态，并通过成人支持和安全回应来对待。"
